  "statement": "Let $W\\subseteq U$ be affine opens with $U\\subseteq V_i\\cap V_j$. Then the\noverlap isomorphism $\\omega_{ij,U}$ of\n[def-nagata-global-blowup-overlap-basic-map] maps\n$\\mathsf B_{V_i}(\\mathcal I)|_W$ onto $\\mathsf B_{V_j}(\\mathcal I)|_W$, and\nits restriction there is $\\omega_{ij,W}$. In particular, the overlap\nisomorphisms constructed from two affine opens $U,U'\\subseteq V_i\\cap V_j$\nagree over every affine open $W\\subseteq U\\cap U'$.",
  "proof": [
   {
    "text": "The transition morphisms of [def-nagata-global-blowup-local-model] form a\nfunctor, so $r_{V,W}=r_{V,U}\\circ r_{U,W}$ for $V=V_i,V_j$ (this is\n[lemma-nagata-affine-blowup-restrict-cocycle]). Hence\n$\\omega_{ij,U}\\circ r_{V_i,W}=r_{V_j,U}\\circ r_{V_i,U}^{-1}\\circ\nr_{V_i,U}\\circ r_{U,W}=r_{V_j,W}$. Since $r_{V_i,W}$ and $r_{V_j,W}$ are\nisomorphisms onto $\\mathsf B_{V_i}(\\mathcal I)|_W$ and\n$\\mathsf B_{V_j}(\\mathcal I)|_W$, the morphism $\\omega_{ij,U}$ maps the\nfirst onto the second and agrees there with\n$r_{V_j,W}\\circ r_{V_i,W}^{-1}=\\omega_{ij,W}$. Applying this to $U$ and to\n$U'$ gives the last assertion.",
    "uses": [
     "def-nagata-global-blowup-local-model",
     "lemma-nagata-affine-blowup-restrict-cocycle"
    ],
    "elementary": false
   }
  ],
